# PROVENANCE: measured from a factory-fresh genuine DESFire EV3 2K with Proxmark3 on 2026-11-01
# (random UID). Same card and batch as hardware_physical_ev3_2k_value_rights.vec.
# PROVISIONAL BATCH "value-rights-2026-11-01": carries `capture-batch: value-rights-2026-11-01` and
# `capture-status: provisional`, so it can be thrown away with the rest of the batch if the card
# proves faulty (see docs/capture-batches.md).
#
# What this measures: how CreateStdDataFile, CreateBackupDataFile, CreateLinearRecordFile and
# CreateValueFile treat each unusual communication byte, then what GetFileSettings reports for
# the files the card agreed to create (no authentication: the application allows free creation).
# Observed:
#   * 0x40 and 0x43 (the SDM flag set at creation) are refused: 9D for a standard data file, 9E
#     for the other three types.
#   * 0x04 (a reserved mode bit) is refused with 9E on every type.
#   * 0x02 (mode 2) is accepted on every type and reported back as 02.
#   * 0x80 (the additional-access-rights flag) is accepted on every type and reported back as 80,
#     with one extra zero byte, the count of additional access rights, after the settings.
name: genuine EV3 2K file creation with unusual communication bytes (provisional batch)
case-id: hardware-physical-ev3-2k-create-comm-bytes
origin: physical-card
capture-batch: value-rights-2026-11-01
capture-status: provisional
feature-version: 6
source: physical-card-proxmark3
requires: backup-files,record-files
uid: 04112233445566
picc-generation: EV3
picc-storage: 2048
picc-key-settings-1: 0F
picc-key-settings-2: 01
picc-key-len: 16
picc-auth-mode: D40
picc-hardware-version: 04010133001605
picc-software-version: 04010103001605

# fixture: application 123456 with two keys
field-off
scan
exchange native CA1234560F02 => 00
exchange native 5A123456 => 00

# CreateFile with communication byte 40: standard data, backup data, linear record and value files
field-off
scan
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange native CD0140EEEE100000 => 9D
exchange native CB0240EEEE100000 => 9E
exchange native C10340EEEE040000020000 => 9E
exchange native CC0440EEEE00000000E80300006400000000 => 9E

# CreateFile with communication byte 43: standard data, backup data, linear record and value files
field-off
scan
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange native CD0543EEEE100000 => 9D
exchange native CB0643EEEE100000 => 9E
exchange native C10743EEEE040000020000 => 9E
exchange native CC0843EEEE00000000E80300006400000000 => 9E

# CreateFile with communication byte 04: standard data, backup data, linear record and value files
field-off
scan
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange native CD0904EEEE100000 => 9E
exchange native CB0A04EEEE100000 => 9E
exchange native C10B04EEEE040000020000 => 9E
exchange native CC0C04EEEE00000000E80300006400000000 => 9E

# CreateFile with communication byte 80: standard data, backup data, linear record and value files
field-off
scan
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange native CD0D80EEEE100000 => 00
exchange native CB0E80EEEE100000 => 00
exchange native C10F80EEEE040000020000 => 00
exchange native CC1080EEEE00000000E80300006400000000 => 00

# CreateFile with communication byte 02: standard data, backup data, linear record and value files
field-off
scan
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange native CD1102EEEE100000 => 00
exchange native CB1202EEEE100000 => 00
exchange native C11302EEEE040000020000 => 00
exchange native CC1402EEEE00000000E80300006400000000 => 00

# GetFileSettings of every file the card agreed to create
field-off
scan
exchange native 5A123456 => 00
exchange native F50D => 000080EEEE10000000
exchange native F50E => 000180EEEE10000000
exchange native F50F => 000380EEEE04000002000000000000
exchange native F510 => 000280EEEE00000000E8030000000000000000
exchange native F511 => 000002EEEE100000
exchange native F512 => 000102EEEE100000
exchange native F513 => 000302EEEE040000020000000000
exchange native F514 => 000202EEEE00000000E80300000000000000
